Paid Birth Recovery Leave provides **four weeks of paid leave per year** [2].  

Eligibility is limited to **full‑time, regular faculty or staff members who**  
* have completed **two full calendar years of employment** in an active status (including nine‑ or ten‑month appointments) [8];  
* are the **birth parent** [8]; and  
* are **eligible for Family and Medical Leave (FMLA)** – which requires at least **12 months of service** and **1,250 hours worked in the preceding 12 months** [8];  

These employees must also be eligible for FMLA and give birth [2].
